<% content_for :title, "Trusted Sources" %>

<div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Trusted Sources</h1>
  <p class="text-xl text-slate-400 mb-8">
    Push your own verdicts into phish.directory instead of asking us for ours.
  </p>

  <p class="text-slate-400 mb-6">
    Every other endpoint answers the question "what do you know about this value?".
    The trusted source endpoints answer the opposite one. You already know, and we
    record what you tell us. A submission creates the record if we have never seen
    the value, and replaces its verdict if we have. Our upstream checks do not run.
  </p>

  <div class="bg-pd-secondary border border-slate-700/20 rounded-xl p-4 not-prose mb-8">
    <div class="font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-1">Base URL</div>
    <code class="text-cyan-accent">https://phish.directory/api</code>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Access</h2>

  <p class="text-slate-400 mb-4">
    These endpoints need a service key marked as a trusted source. A user API key
    (<code class="text-cyan-accent">pdat_*</code>) cannot call them, whatever the
    user's access level. Ask us to mark one of your service keys as a trusted
    source. We recommend a separate key from the one you read with, so you can
    revoke ingestion without losing lookups.
  </p>

  <p class="text-slate-400 mb-8">
    A request from any other key returns
    <code class="text-cyan-accent">403 Forbidden</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Endpoints</h2>

  <div class="not-prose space-y-4 mb-8">
    <div class="bg-pd-secondary border border-slate-700/20 rounded-xl p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
        <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-blue-500/15 text-blue-500 rounded font-mono text-xs font-semibold">POST</span>
        <code class="text-slate-100 font-mono">/v1/source/domains</code>
      </div>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm mb-4">Upsert domains and their verdicts.</p>

      <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Parameters</div>
      <table class="w-full text-sm mb-4">
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">domains</code></td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-slate-500">array</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4"><span class="text-red-400 text-xs">required</span></td>
          <td class="py-2 text-slate-400">Strings, or objects. Max 1000 per request.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">classification</code></td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-slate-500">string</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4"><span class="text-slate-500 text-xs">optional</span></td>
          <td class="py-2 text-slate-400">Applies to every entry that states none of its own.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">confidence</code></td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-slate-500">number</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4"><span class="text-slate-500 text-xs">optional</span></td>
          <td class="py-2 text-slate-400">0 to 1. Defaults to 1.0.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>

      <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Example Request</div>
      <div class="bg-pd-tertiary rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-sm mb-4">
<pre class="text-slate-100">{
  "domains": [
    { "domain": "evil.example", "classification": "phishing", "confidence": 0.99 },
    { "domain": "unsure.example", "classification": "suspicious" }
  ]
}</pre>
      </div>

      <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Example Response</div>
      <div class="bg-pd-tertiary rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-sm">
<pre class="text-slate-100">{
  "results": [
    {
      "value": "evil.example",
      "status": "created",
      "id": "dom_4k8xJm2pN9qW",
      "classification": "phishing",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "verdict_id": "vrd_7fQ2xR4tL1mZ"
    },
    {
      "value": "unsure.example",
      "status": "updated",
      "id": "dom_9pW3kL6nT2vB",
      "classification": "suspicious",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "verdict_id": "vrd_2mN8jH5qC7xD"
    }
  ],
  "counts": { "created": 1, "updated": 1 },
  "count": 2
}</pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-pd-secondary border border-slate-700/20 rounded-xl p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
        <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-blue-500/15 text-blue-500 rounded font-mono text-xs font-semibold">POST</span>
        <code class="text-slate-100 font-mono">/v1/source/urls</code>
      </div>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm mb-4">
        Same shape. The array parameter is <code class="text-cyan-accent">urls</code>
        and an object entry carries <code class="text-cyan-accent">url</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-pd-secondary border border-slate-700/20 rounded-xl p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
        <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-blue-500/15 text-blue-500 rounded font-mono text-xs font-semibold">POST</span>
        <code class="text-slate-100 font-mono">/v1/source/emails</code>
      </div>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm mb-4">
        Same shape. The array parameter is <code class="text-cyan-accent">emails</code>
        and an object entry carries <code class="text-cyan-accent">email</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-pd-secondary border border-slate-700/20 rounded-xl p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
        <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-blue-500/15 text-blue-500 rounded font-mono text-xs font-semibold">POST</span>
        <code class="text-slate-100 font-mono">/v1/source/phone_numbers</code>
      </div>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm mb-4">
        Same shape. The array parameter is
        <code class="text-cyan-accent">phone_numbers</code> and an object entry
        carries <code class="text-cyan-accent">phone_number</code>. Numbers must be
        in E.164 format, for example <code class="text-cyan-accent">+14155551234</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Entry Shape</h2>

  <p class="text-slate-400 mb-4">
    An entry is either a bare string or an object. A bare string takes the
    request-level <code class="text-cyan-accent">classification</code> and
    <code class="text-cyan-accent">confidence</code>, so a feed with one
    classification does not repeat itself:
  </p>

  <div class="bg-pd-tertiary rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-sm mb-6 not-prose">
<pre class="text-slate-100">{
  "classification": "phishing",
  "domains": ["evil.example", "worse.example"]
}</pre>
  </div>

  <p class="text-slate-400 mb-4">An object entry accepts these fields:</p>

  <table class="w-full text-sm mb-8 not-prose">
    <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
      <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">domain</code> / <code class="text-cyan-accent">url</code> / <code class="text-cyan-accent">email</code> / <code class="text-cyan-accent">phone_number</code></td>
      <td class="py-2 text-slate-400">The value. <code class="text-cyan-accent">value</code> also works.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
      <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">classification</code></td>
      <td class="py-2 text-slate-400">Overrides the request-level one.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
      <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">confidence</code></td>
      <td class="py-2 text-slate-400">0 to 1.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
      <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">metadata</code></td>
      <td class="py-2 text-slate-400">Free-form object stored on the verdict. Max 4KB of JSON.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Classifications</h2>

  <p class="text-slate-400 mb-4">
    A trusted source may send <code class="text-cyan-accent">phishing</code>,
    <code class="text-cyan-accent">suspicious</code> or
    <code class="text-cyan-accent">clean</code>.
  </p>

  <p class="text-slate-400 mb-8">
    <code class="text-cyan-accent">unknown</code> is refused, because it carries no
    information and would only overwrite a verdict we already hold.
    <code class="text-cyan-accent">protected</code> is refused too: the protected
    list is our own operators' decision, and a source cannot hand it out.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Per-entry Results</h2>

  <p class="text-slate-400 mb-4">
    One bad entry does not fail the request. Every entry gets its own result, and
    the response is <code class="text-cyan-accent">200 OK</code> as long as the
    request itself was well formed. Each result carries a status:
  </p>

  <table class="w-full text-sm mb-8 not-prose">
    <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
      <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">created</code></td>
      <td class="py-2 text-slate-400">We had never seen this value. The record and its verdict are new.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
      <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">updated</code></td>
      <td class="py-2 text-slate-400">We already held the value. Its verdict now says what you sent.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
      <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">invalid</code></td>
      <td class="py-2 text-slate-400">Malformed value, classification or confidence. See <code class="text-cyan-accent">reason</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
      <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">rejected</code></td>
      <td class="py-2 text-slate-400">The value is on our protected list, so nothing was written.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <p class="text-slate-400 mb-8">
    The request itself returns <code class="text-cyan-accent">400 Bad Request</code>
    when the array is missing, empty, or holds more than 1000 entries.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Attribution</h2>

  <p class="text-slate-400 mb-8">
    Every verdict you write names your service as its source, so anyone reading the
    record can see who classified it. Resubmitting the same value replaces the
    verdict in place. Nothing is duplicated, so you can push the same feed as often
    as you like.
  </p>
</div>
